course: dictionary
lesson: 7021
title: A sudden burst
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: A paroxysm is a sudden, strong burst of a feeling or action that you cannot control. It does not mean a small feeling. It arrives all at once and takes over. «A paroxysm of laughter» means you suddenly laugh so hard you cannot stop.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «In his violent paroxysms» the word violent tells you the burst is strong and wild, and the brackets say fits. Try the swap: «In his violent fits» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Doctors use the word too. Whooping cough causes paroxysms of coughing, which means sudden bouts of coughing that come on hard and fast. It is the same idea in a different place: a sudden attack that comes on strong.
fact: Paroxysm is a noun, so you can have one, or several: paroxysms.
fact: «Paroxysm» means a sudden, strong burst of feeling or action that you cannot control.
fact: In medicine, a paroxysm is a sudden attack or worsening of an illness, such as a fit of coughing.
fact: «Paroxysm» is often used with «of», as in «a paroxysm of laughter» or «a paroxysm of rage».
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad has violent paroxysms, and he acts them out with bedroom chairs, noises and a somersault.
exercise: «She fell into a paroxysm of laughter at the joke.» What is a paroxysm here? | A quiet smile | A cup of tea | *A sudden, strong burst of laughing that you cannot stop | A long, slow walk
exercise: In medicine, what is a paroxysm? | A steady, healthy heartbeat | A bandage for a cut | *A sudden attack or worsening of an illness, such as a fit of coughing | A kind of medicine you swallow with water
exercise: «In his violent paroxysms» Toad acts out a wild fit. Which word in this clue shows the burst is strong? | *Violent | Somersault | Chairs | Bedroom
test: «A paroxysm of rage» could be swapped for «a ___ of rage» without changing the meaning. Which word fits the gap? | Nap | *Fit | Whisper | Garden
test: Whooping cough causes paroxysms of coughing. What does this tell you? | Coughing never happens | The cough is a kind of food | The cough is quiet and steady all day | *Coughing comes in sudden, hard bursts
exam: Ella says a paroxysm is a small, quiet feeling. What is the correct meaning? | *A sudden, strong burst you cannot control | A slow walk through a quiet garden | A small, calm thought before bed | A type of bedroom chair
